# Nuxt Path Aliases

## Overview

Nuxt provides predefined aliases to simplify imports and avoid messy relative paths. Always use these aliases instead of relative path navigation (e.g., `../../../`).

## Available Aliases

```typescript
{
  "~": "/<srcDir>",        // Source directory (app folder)
  "@": "/<srcDir>",        // Source directory (app folder)
  "~~": "/<rootDir>",      // Project root
  "@@": "/<rootDir>",      // Project root
  "#shared": "/<rootDir>/shared",
  "assets": "/<srcDir>/assets",
  "public": "/<rootDir>/public",
  "#build": "/<rootDir>/.nuxt",
  "#internal/nuxt/paths": "/<rootDir>/.nuxt/paths.mjs"
}
```

## Usage Guidelines

### Frontend Code (app/ folder)

Use `@` or `~` to import from the source directory:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { something } from '@/components/MyComponent.vue'
import { util } from '@/utils/helpers'

// ❌ BAD - Don't use relative paths
import { something } from '../../../components/MyComponent.vue'
```

**Note:** In webpack contexts (image sources, CSS), prefix with `~`:
```vue
<style>
.background {
  background-image: url('~assets/image.png');
}
</style>
```

### Backend Code (server/ folder)

Use `@@` to import from the project root, then navigate to `server/`:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Use @@ alias
import { generatePrefixedId } from '@@/server/utils/id-generator'
import { extractLogContext } from '@@/server/utils/logger'
import { handleApiError } from '@@/server/utils/error-handler'

// ❌ BAD - Don't use relative paths drilling up
import { generatePrefixedId } from '../../../../../utils/id-generator'
import { extractLogContext } from '../../utils/logger'
```

## Why This Matters

1. **Maintainability**: Moving files doesn't break imports
2. **Readability**: Clear where imports come from (`@@/server/` vs `../../../`)
3. **Type Safety**: Aliases are automatically added to TypeScript configs
4. **Consistency**: Team-wide standard for import paths

## Examples from Codebase

### ✅ Correct Usage

From `server/api/career-id/profile/[profileId]/certifications/[id].delete.ts`:
```typescript
import { extractLogContext } from '@@/server/utils/logger'
```

### ❌ Incorrect Usage

From `server/api/career-id/profile/[profileId]/contact/index.post.ts`:
```typescript
import { generatePrefixedId } from '../../../../../utils/id-generator'
// Should be: import { generatePrefixedId } from '@@/server/utils/id-generator'
```

## Reference

See [Nuxt Alias Documentation](https://nuxt.com/docs/api/nuxt-config#alias) for more details.
